# Files: scripts/__tests__/sdlc-deliver.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/293-persist-exact-head-delivery-cas-and-isolated-session-tokens/requirements.md
Feature: Persist exact-head delivery CAS and isolated session tokens
  Delivery previously rediscovered live PR identity and allowed unscoped canonical-state mutation.
  This was fixed by scoped state namespaces and a CAS-bound expected PR/head.

  # --- Exact Head Through Merge ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Delivery merges and completes only at the persisted expected head
    Given controller-owned delivery has CAS-persisted expected PR P and head H
    When readiness and merge complete
    Then every snapshot and merge uses P at H
    And the passed handoff requires P MERGED at H and the issue CLOSED

  # --- Stable Reconciliation ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Unexpected PR or head identity records one terminal reconciliation failure
    Given delivery expects PR P at head H
    When P is merged at another head or changes outside an authorized transition
    Then delivery persists delivery_reconciliation_required with expected and observed identity
    And subsequent invocations return the same failure without another PR mutation

  # --- Isolated Standalone Session ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: Standalone delivery cannot overwrite another issue's canonical checkpoint
    Given issue A owns the canonical checkpoint
    When standalone open-pr for issue B uses a dedicated session token
    Then B writes only its session run state and handoff paths
    And A's canonical checkpoint and handoff bytes remain unchanged
    And an unscoped delivery is rejected before mutation

  # --- Normal Path Preserved ---

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: Matching scoped delivery still reaches terminal proof
    Given a scoped delivery whose live PR remains at the expected head
    When required checks and review evidence pass
    Then exact-head squash merge and issue closure complete
    And the controller writes a passed deliver handoff

  # --- Existing PR Version Publication ---

  @SCN005 @regression
  Scenario: Existing PR rebinds only to the controller-owned version head
    Given delivery has persisted an existing exact-branch PR at H1
    When clean version publication pushes current local head H2
    Then delivery re-reads the persisted PR after the push
    And expected head advances to H2 only when that PR remains open, its PR number and exact issue branch match independently, and its head equals clean local HEAD
    And merge never uses pre-bump H1
    And a foreign remote head records delivery_reconciliation_required

  # --- Multi-Issue Live Worker Resume ---

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Execute restores the next issue branch before matching a live retained worker
    Given an earlier delivered issue left a clean multi-issue checkout on the default branch
    And the next non-start worker is live with exact issue-branch and head ownership
    When execute resumes the next issue
    Then execute restores the expected active issue branch before ownership matching
    And the exact live worker resumes without retained_worker_mismatch
    And dirty or foreign work is never overwritten
